# Constraint & Violation Log

**Purpose:**
This file records real moments where scope, architecture, or discipline was tested during development. It is used later to extract hard constraints for phase-specific AI agent prompts.

**Rules:**
- This file is append-only
- Log every temptation to skip ahead
- Log every undocumented decision
- Log every moment where discipline mattered
- Log every architectural ambiguity that forced a choice

**Format:**
```
[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] VIOLATION_TYPE
Phase: v0.X
Wanted: <what you tried to do>
Blocked: Yes/No
Rationale: <why it violated scope or why decision was needed>
Outcome: <what happened>
---
```

---

## Log Entries

[2025-01-06 16:00] PROJECT_INITIALIZATION
Phase: v0.1
Action: Created spec-kit (README, ARCHITECTURE, SCOPE, DECISIONS, FRAMEWORK, CORE)
Status: Complete
Notes: Foundation documents established. Ready to begin implementation.
---

[2025-01-06 18:30] BUG_DISCOVERED
Phase: v0.1
Component: probe/core/map.py
Issue: SQLite transaction error in add_entity() and other insert methods
Root Cause: Calling commit() before fetchone() with RETURNING clause
Fix: Fetch result before committing transaction
Impact: Blocked all entity/document/page/edge insertion
Resolution: Updated all add_* methods to fetch before commit
Lesson: SQLite with row_factory requires careful transaction ordering
